  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"939\" data-end=\"1026\">\n<p data-start=\"941\" data-end=\"1026\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"941\" data-end=\"976\">CMV IgG Positive &amp; IgM Positive</strong> may indicate <strong data-start=\"990\" data-end=\"1025\">recent or reactivated infection</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1027\" data-end=\"1156\">\n<p data-start=\"1029\" data-end=\"1156\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1029\" data-end=\"1046\">Avidity Index</strong> helps differentiate between <strong data-start=\"1075\" data-end=\"1103\">recent primary infection</strong> (low avidity) vs. <strong data-start=\"1122\" data-end=\"1140\">past infection</strong> (high avidity).</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1157\" data-end=\"1319\">\n<p data-start=\"1159\" data-end=\"1319\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Important in <strong data-start=\"1172\" data-end=\"1185\">pregnancy</strong>, transplant candidates, and immunocompromised patients to assess <strong data-start=\"1251\" data-end=\"1290\">risk of congenital CMV transmission</strong> or <strong data-start=\"1294\" data-end=\"1318\">disease reactivation</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1320\" data-end=\"1400\">\n<p data-start=\"1322\" data-end=\"1400\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1322\" data-end=\"1337\">Low avidity</strong> IgG with <strong data-start=\"1347\" data-end=\"1363\">positive IgM</strong> suggests recent (primary) infection.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1401\" data-end=\"1489\">\n<p data-start=\"1403\" data-end=\"1489\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1403\" data-end=\"1419\">High avidity</strong> IgG with <strong data-start=\"1429\" data-end=\"1445\">positive IgM</strong> usually rules out recent primary infection.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
